    "aboutDish": "Paneer Butter Masala is a rich North Indian curry made with paneer, tomato, butter, cream, and aromatic spices. It is believed to have originated around the Delhi and Punjab region, inspired by popular restaurant-style tomato-butter gravies. Today, it is widely eaten across India and in Indian restaurants around the world as a popular vegetarian dish.",

